<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<task id="010" project="code-quality-and-assurance-r4">
  <metadata>
    <title>Classify all 49 ADRs on three axes and grow INDEX.md from 36 to 49</title>
    <phase>2a Every ADR is routed, accurate, and measured</phase>
    <gate>startable</gate>
    <status>not-started</status>
    <rigor>FULL</rigor>
    <rigor-reason>Architectural classification with repo-wide blast radius — the enforceability and accuracy verdicts decide what P2b enforces and what FR-08 blocks from enforcement. A wrong "current" verdict causes a stale rule to be enforced in CI.</rigor-reason>
    <model-tier>opus</model-tier>
    <model-tier-reason>Judgment-dense architectural reading across 49 ADRs; the accuracy axis requires deciding whether each ADR still describes the code as it is, which is exactly the reasoning Sonnet is not tiered for (CLAUDE.md §8.5 — architectural / ADR-migration work).</model-tier-reason>
    <effort>xhigh</effort>
    <parallel-group>none</parallel-group>
    <parallel-safe>false</parallel-safe>
    <parallel-reason>Writes .claude/adr/INDEX.md — sub-agents cannot write to .claude/ paths (root CLAUDE.md §3). Reading and analysis may be fanned out; the write is main-session only.</parallel-reason>
    <deps>none</deps>
    <tags>adr,governance,classification,docs</tags>
    <estimated-effort>6-8 hours</estimated-effort>
  </metadata>

  <prompt>Classify every one of the 49 ADRs on three axes — enforceability, accuracy, and (for judgment-only ADRs) checkability — recording one line of reason per axis in .claude/adr/INDEX.md. INDEX.md grows from 36 to 49 entries as a side effect, because 13 ADRs exist as files but are absent from the index.</prompt>
  <role>SPAARKE platform architect. Read each ADR against the code it governs before assigning an accuracy verdict. Conservative: when unsure whether an ADR is current, mark it contested rather than guessing current.</role>
  <goal>All 49 ADRs classified on (a) enforceability: enforceable | partially-enforceable | judgment-only; (b) accuracy: current | stale | contested; (c) for judgment-only only: checkable-by-reading | aesthetic — each with one line of reason, recorded in INDEX.md, which now lists 49 entries.</goal>

  <context>
    <background>spec.md FR-05. Enforcement today is 7 of 49, but nobody knows the denominator's shape: which ADRs COULD be enforced mechanically, which are still accurate, and which are judgment calls that no test could ever assert. Without that, "7/49 enforced" reads as failure when the honest framing may be "49/49 routed". This classification produces the routing input for FR-06, the exclusion list for FR-08, and the candidate pool for FR-07. Measured 2026-09-04: 49 ADR files exist; INDEX.md lists 36.</background>
    <relevant-files>
      <file role="modify">.claude/adr/INDEX.md</file>
      <file role="canonical-reference">.claude/adr/</file>
      <file role="canonical-reference">tests/Spaarke.ArchTests/</file>
    </relevant-files>
    <dependencies>
      <dependency task="none" status="complete">Independent. Task 003's citation counts help prioritise reading order but are not required.</dependency>
    </dependencies>
  </context>

  <constraints>
    <constraint source="spec">Scope (all 49): every ADR gets all applicable axes with one line of reason each. An ADR classified without a reason is incomplete — the reason is what makes the verdict reviewable.</constraint>
    <constraint source="spec">Scope (third axis): the checkable-by-reading / aesthetic axis applies ONLY to judgment-only ADRs. Do not assign it to enforceable or partially-enforceable ADRs.</constraint>
    <constraint source="spec">Scope (accuracy axis): "current" means the ADR still describes the code as it is TODAY. Verify against code before asserting it — an ADR that is merely well-written is not thereby current.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Scope (this task): classification ONLY. Do NOT write any arch test, do NOT amend any ADR, do NOT act on a stale verdict. Task 011 routes, task 012 records §6.5 paths, P2b writes tests.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Scope (INDEX.md): add the 13 missing entries so the index lists all 49. Do not remove or renumber existing entries.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Scope (.claude/ write): main-session only. Analysis may be fanned out to sub-agents, but they cannot write here and will fail with "Edit denied" if dispatched to do so.</constraint>
  </constraints>

  <knowledge>
    <topic>ADR classification and enforcement routing</topic>
    <files>
      <file>.claude/adr/INDEX.md</file>
      <file>.claude/adr/ADR-038-testing-strategy.md</file>
      <file>docs/standards/TEST-ARCHITECTURE.md</file>
      <file>projects/code-quality-and-assurance-r4/spec.md</file>
      <file>CLAUDE.md</file>
    </files>
    <patterns>
      <pattern name="Existing arch tests as enforceability evidence" location="tests/Spaarke.ArchTests/">An ADR already carrying a test is demonstrably enforceable. Check this directory before classifying — some ADRs may be enforced by unnamed guards, which changes the verdict.</pattern>
    </patterns>
  </knowledge>

  <steps mode="directional">
    <step order="0" name="Context + rigor declaration">Output the rigor-level declaration (FULL + reason). Enumerate the 49 ADR files and diff against INDEX.md's 36 entries to identify the 13 missing.</step>
    <step order="1">Inventory tests/Spaarke.ArchTests/ and map each existing test to the ADR it enforces. An ADR enforced by an unnamed guard is still enforced — record which.</step>
    <step order="2">For each ADR, assign enforceability with one line of reason: can a mechanical test assert this rule at all?</step>
    <step order="3">For each ADR, assign accuracy with one line of reason, verified against current code. Mark contested rather than current when the evidence is ambiguous.</step>
    <step order="4">For judgment-only ADRs only, assign checkable-by-reading or aesthetic with one line of reason.</step>
    <step order="5">Write all three axes into INDEX.md and add the 13 missing entries so it lists 49.</step>
    <step order="6">Produce a summary in notes/: counts per axis value, and the explicit list of stale and contested ADRs handed to task 012.</step>
    <step order="7">Update TASK-INDEX.md: set task 010 status to ✅.</step>
    <step order="8">Document any deviation in projects/code-quality-and-assurance-r4/notes/.</step>
  </steps>

  <escalation>
    <trigger>If an ADR appears to conflict with another ADR (not merely with code), STOP and escalate per CLAUDE.md §6.5. Two ADRs disagreeing is a governance defect that classification cannot resolve, and picking a winner silently is exactly the failure mode §6.5 exists to prevent.</trigger>
    <trigger>If the file count is not 49 or INDEX.md's entry count is not 36, STOP and report before classifying. The spec's denominator is load-bearing for FR-09a's n/49 reporting, and a changed count means the baseline moved.</trigger>
    <trigger>If more than roughly a third of ADRs classify as stale or contested, STOP and report before continuing. That would indicate the governance surface has drifted far enough that FR-08's per-ADR §6.5 records become a project of their own rather than a step in task 012.</trigger>
  </escalation>

  <outputs>
    <output type="doc">.claude/adr/INDEX.md</output>
    <output type="doc">projects/code-quality-and-assurance-r4/notes/adr-classification-2026-09.md</output>
  </outputs>

  <acceptance-criteria>
    <criterion testable="true">Given INDEX.md, it lists exactly 49 ADR entries.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Given each of the 49, an enforceability value and a one-line reason are recorded.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Given each of the 49, an accuracy value and a one-line reason are recorded.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Given each judgment-only ADR, a checkability value and a one-line reason are recorded.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Negative: no enforceable or partially-enforceable ADR carries a checkability value.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Negative: no arch test is written and no ADR is amended by this task.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">The notes summary lists every stale and contested ADR explicitly, as task 012's input.</criterion>
  </acceptance-criteria>

  <notes>Maps spec.md FR-05. Spec assumption worth testing here: ADR-028 (auth, 1,521 citations) may already be effectively enforced by unnamed auth guards — step 1 determines this, and the answer changes whether P2b needs a test for it. Feeds task 011 (routing), task 012 (§6.5 records), and task 020 (criterion sizing).</notes>

  <execution><skill>.claude/skills/task-execute/SKILL.md</skill></execution>
</task>
